diff --git a/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/dmop.md b/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/dmop.md
--- a/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/dmop.md
+++ b/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/dmop.md
@@ -1,4 +1,22 @@
 # Discounted MOP
+
+The original `stop_gradient_decorator` uses the selected ancestors' log weights
+to correct derivatives through resampling. The added
+`discounted_stop_gradient_decorator` uses the same resampling interface and
+multiplies that derivative correction by `alpha`. The correction is zero in
+the forward calculation. It does not change particle selection, propagation
+or observation likelihoods.
+
+`log_likelihood` constructs the original `particle_filter.build_filter` with
+this decorator. Its internal loop calls the original PF update functions and
+returns only the terminal state, with optional rematerialization for gradients.
+`fit` differentiates this objective and calls a caller-supplied optimizer.
+The optimizer is not an ADPF implementation and does not replace the PF.
+
+At `alpha=1`, the derivative agrees with the original ADPF correction. For
+`alpha<1`, it is a discounted derivative, not the ordinary derivative of the
+unchanged forward likelihood. This extension is restricted to pathwise
+differentiable bootstrap models with resampling at every observation.
 
 ::: cuthbert.smc.dmop
 
diff --git a/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/ifad.md b/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/ifad.md
--- a/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/ifad.md
+++ b/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/ifad.md
@@ -1,3 +1,13 @@
 # IFAD
 
+`fit` composes `iterated_filtering.fit` and `dmop.fit`, then evaluates the final
+parameters with independent original bootstrap PF draws. All three calls use
+the same model factory. IF2 supplies the starting parameters for a newly
+initialized optimizer in the DMOP stage; the stages have separate random keys.
+
+This module does not implement another particle filter. It delegates fitting
+to the two modules above and scoring to `particle_filter.build_filter` with an
+ordinary resampler. Parameter transformations stay in the model factory;
+perturbation scales and optimizer settings are supplied through the API.
+
 ::: cuthbert.smc.ifad
diff --git a/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/iterated_filtering.md b/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/iterated_filtering.md
--- a/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/iterated_filtering.md
+++ b/docs/api_cuthbert/smc/iterated_filtering.md
@@ -1,3 +1,20 @@
 # Iterated filtering
 
+`fit` adds Gaussian parameter perturbations and repeated passes through the
+data to the existing bootstrap PF. A model factory returns the same initial,
+propagation and observation callbacks accepted by `particle_filter.build_filter`.
+The factory applies any parameter transformations; it does not implement IF2.
+
+The module wraps those callbacks so that each particle contains both the model
+state and its parameters. It calls the original PF update with these augmented
+particles. State and parameters are resampled together. The complete terminal
+parameter swarm, rather than just its mean, is passed to the next iteration.
+Initial and within-pass perturbation scales can be specified separately.
+
+The implementation uses the original `filter_prepare`, `filter_combine` and
+systematic or multinomial resampler. Its time loop stores only the terminal
+filter state. The model callbacks do not need their own perturbation logic.
+This interface currently supports unconditional bootstrap resampling and a
+geometric cooling factor between passes; other schedules are not implied.
+
 ::: cuthbert.smc.iterated_filtering
